All 15 tests pass. Here's the summary of every bug fixed:

**`src/auth.py`** (2 bugs):
- `has_permission`: comparison was case-sensitive. Changed to compare `required.lower()` against `(r.lower() for r in user_roles)`.
- `is_admin_or_owner`: used `and` (both conditions required). Changed to `or` so admin OR owner both grant access.

**`src/inventory.py`** (4 bugs):
- `__init__`: mutable default arg `={}` was shared across all instances. Changed to `None` + fresh dict per call.
- `add`: overwrote stock with `self._stock[sku] = qty`. Changed to `self._stock.get(sku, 0) + qty` (accumulate).
- `reserve`: used `>=` in the boundary check, rejecting qty == available. Changed to `>`.
- `release`: no validation on release amount. Added guard: `if qty > current: raise ValueError(...)`.

**`src/text_utils.py`** (3 bugs):
- `slugify`: no lowercasing. Added `.lower()` to the collapsed string.
- `slugify`: `"--"`→`"-"` replacement was single-pass, left `---`→`--`. Switched to `re.sub(r"-+", "-", ...)`.
- `truncate`: sliced at `max_len` then appended suffix, exceeding the limit. Changed to slice at `max_len - len(suffix)`.
